<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="TimerComponents-282F0D26" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic concept/concept ">
<title class="- topic/title ">Timer components</title>
<shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">These components include three types of timers, and two
components for working with Baja absolute time (AbsTime). </shortdesc>
<prolog class="- topic/prolog ">
<metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">timer components</indexterm></keywords>
</metadata>
</prolog>
<conbody class="- topic/body  concept/conbody ">
<p class="- topic/p ">Two of the timers are Boolean-types:</p>
<ul class="- topic/ul ">
<li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">BooleanDelay</p></li>
<li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">OneShot</p></li>
</ul>
<p class="- topic/p ">A third dimer is a Numeric-type: NumericDelay.</p>
<p class="- topic/p ">To work with absolute time, kitControl provides two components:</p>
<ul class="- topic/ul ">
<li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">CurrentTime</p></li>
<li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p ">TimeDifference</p></li>
</ul>
</conbody>
</concept>